    <item>
      <title>What Did Hubble See on Your Birthday?</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/The-EXCITED-State/posts/what-did-hubble-see-on-your-birthday/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 23 Feb 2026 17:24:00 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/The-EXCITED-State/posts/what-did-hubble-see-on-your-birthday/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;alt&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;http://localhost:1313/The-EXCITED-State/posts/what-did-hubble-see-on-your-birthday/figures/hubble.jpg&#34;&gt;
The Hubble Space Telescope captured this image on my birthday in a certain year. The star-forming region, called Sharpless 2-106, looks like a celestial angel. The &amp;ldquo;wings&amp;rdquo; of the nebula are twin lobes of hot gas that stretch outward from a massive, young star near the center of the image.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>ACEE 命题结束</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/The-EXCITED-State/posts/acee-%E5%91%BD%E9%A2%98/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 17 Feb 2026 17:00:00 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/The-EXCITED-State/posts/acee-%E5%91%BD%E9%A2%98/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;从构思到题目落地，前前后后花了十多天时间，改了又改，花了我很多心血。希望能有一些挑战，同时也不会过多为难完成报名表的勇士们。有时候真实地感到自己知识的匮乏，以及学过东西的快速遗忘，命题的过程也是我自己学习的过程。题出得好不好，可能也得交给做题者来评判。等到招生结束，我也许会把题目挂在这里，供路过者批评。&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
